<p>NOTE: Full name is Billing Information Concepts Corp.  </p>
<p>(1) Earnings per share and weighted average shares outstanding for the quarter and six-month period ended March 31, 1996 are presented on a pro forma basis and give effect to the shares assumed to be issued had the spin-off from USLD occurred at the beginning of the periods presented.</p>
<p>The comparison of revenues and earnings in the second quarters of both fiscal years is affected by the large volume of call processing and customer service inquiries related to a certain customer's business during 1996 Q2. The transactions related to the customer resulted in one-time revenues of about $1.8 million and one-time earnings per share of about $0.04 in the quarter. Excluding these gains, revenues and earnings per share for the quarter would have been about $25.1 million and $0.29, respectively.</p>
